WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.800
1909: begin from traceable railway evidence.

00:03.800 --> 00:05.900
Present: everyday arrival and public service remain on the same line of responsibility.

00:05.900 --> 00:08.000
Future: provenance, human responsibility, and an exit route stay visible.

00:08.000 --> 00:17.000
Railway rhythm becomes a low-impact, enterable public corridor.

00:17.000 --> 00:26.000
Roof trusses and mileage indices become learning, archives, and a minimal credential.

00:26.000 --> 00:29.500
The minimal learning credential enters a pausable AI-assistance layer.

00:29.500 --> 00:33.500
A human confirms high-impact decisions; AI does not issue the final public-service decision.

00:33.500 --> 00:37.000
With AI off, ordinary service, human handoff, and offline exit remain available.

00:37.000 --> 00:42.000
Human confirmation enters controlled validation; no real green or passed state is implied.

00:42.000 --> 00:45.500
Validation can pause; physical stops and human responsibility remain visible.

00:45.500 --> 00:48.000
Exit, recovery, and return to ordinary use remain independent of validation results.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.000
Four chapters, five stations, M1–M4, three zones/two wings × eight resource axes: concept-bounded, human-final, always exitable.
